## Sprint-audit — Signal 11

**`/home/marielle/projects/bathos/src/bathos/sprint_audit.py`** — claim Signal 11 (the numbering gap between Signal 10 at ~line 521-524 and Signal 12 at ~line 526-540), inserted between them, following Signal 13's exact dispatch template (`db.execute` scan of confirmation/sequential campaigns with a registered claim, try/except-wrapped, appended to `anomalies`, ~line 542-595):

```python
# Signal 11: differential-staleness — positive_control clauses reported
# uncontrolled by differential_confound_check (invalid_measurement outcome or
# dependency-lock drift since the differential ran) on confirmation/sequential
# campaigns that are not open/abandoned.
```
- Iterate the same `confirmation_with_claims`-style query (mode IN confirmation/sequential, status NOT IN open/abandoned, claim_path set), parse each claim, skip if no clause has `positive_control=true`, else call `bathos.claim.differential_confound_check(db, campaign_id, claim, project_root)` and append one anomaly per `status == "uncontrolled"` clause: `f"Confirmation campaign '{cname}' ({cid[:8]}) positive-control clause '{label}' is uncontrolled — instrument-sensitivity proof missing, invalidated by dependency drift, or covering run failed invalid_measurement (differential debt #1071)."`
- Record `signals["differential_staleness_count"]` (count of such anomalies) for the returned `signals` dict, matching the pattern of the other named signals.

